Subject: [PATCH] presentation: draw covers with AsyncImage so grids scroll
 without subcomposition

MangaCover used SubcomposeAsyncImage, which subcomposes every cell of a
lazy grid and gave each loading cell an indeterminate spinner that
animates on every frame. On the panorama staggered grid this showed up
as dropped frames and a jerky fast-scroll thumb, while mihon-harmony
(plain AsyncImage + colour placeholder) scrolled smoothly.

Draw the cover with AsyncImage inside the same coloured box. Loading
and error states keep the KMK look: the error icon is drawn over the
box, and the spinner only appears when a cover is still loading after
400 ms, so memory and disk cache hits never flash one.

SourceIconBadge read Source.icon on every composition; the getter scans
installed extensions and may draw the drawable into a new bitmap. Keep
it per source id.

mihon-harmony does not have this: its MangaCover is already AsyncImage
and it has no source icon badge.
